error[E0277]: `weaveffi::Iter<i32>` can't cross the WeaveFFI C ABI
 --> tests/ui/fail_iter_param.rs:4:21
  |
4 | pub fn drain(items: weaveffi::Iter<i32>) -> i64 {
  |                     ^^^^^^^^ not a WeaveFFI value type
  |
  = help: the trait `weaveffi::rt::types::FfiType<Tag>` is not implemented for `weaveffi::Iter<i32>`
  = note: a value is a scalar (`i32`, `f64`, `bool`, `usize`, ...), `char`, `String`, `Vec<T>`, `Option<T>`, a `HashMap` or `BTreeMap`, a `#[weaveffi::record]`, a `#[weaveffi::enumeration]`, a `#[weaveffi::custom]` type, or a `#[weaveffi::interface]` as `Arc<T>`
  = note: a parameter may also be borrowed (`&str`, `&[T]`, `&T`), and only a whole return may be a `weaveffi::Iter<T>`
  = help: the following other types implement trait `weaveffi::rt::types::FfiType<UT>`:
            BTreeMap<K, V>
            HashMap<K, V>
            Option<T>
            String
            Vec<T>
            bool
            char
            f32
          and $N others

